  "text": "QUESTION TYPE: PEDIATRICS\nCLINICAL CASE:\nA 10-year-old boy with brief episodes of distractions (< 1 minute) in which he does not respond to calls and blinks.\nAn EEG shows spike-wave discharges at 3 cycles per second.\nFirst-line elective treatment would with:\n1- Valproate.\n2- Carbamazepine.\n3- Phenytoin.\n4- Gabapentin.\n5- Clonazepam.\nCORRECT ANSWER: 1\nThe seizures described and the EEG correspond to typical absence seizures and the initial treatment of choice is valproic acid.",
